Z||000000||ayamnik||09-23-1999||11:45 AM||||I reset the Iac and drove for 40 miles at about 60mph. It didn’t help it It idle at 900  and all of a sudden up to 1500 or even 2000. When I stop at a light and have my foot on the brake my trany wont let it idle at more then 1000rpm but the car wont’s to idle higher so it dies. I replaced the IAC and TPS and some other censor that has a wiring connection to it and one vacuum tube and the injector it self. I have no vacuum licks. All this at normal temperature. Can any one help? I love my car and I cant do or think about anything when it not running good. Help||||reg||9
Z||000001||mwbackus||09-23-1999||12:11 PM||||A new IAC valve will set a code 24 (vehicle speed sensor) before it learns all the new settings. The result is exactly as you describe.  Reset the ECM again at home, and bring the bat. terminal removal wrench with you on your "training" drive (only needs to be a couple miles at 40 mph).  Carefully watch the check engine light to determine when the code 24 is set, the idle will also reveal this.  Then pull over to the side of the road and reset it once again.<P>Mike||||reg||1
Z||000002||ayamnik||09-23-1999||12:20 PM||||One little thing I forgot it doesn’t give me code 24 it flashes 35 with is iac but it’s brand-new? I’ll reset it one more time today at lunch. Any other suggestions.||||reg||1
Z||000003||theogre||09-23-1999||02:16 PM||||look for vacuum leaks. look again.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Kage86GT4SP||09-23-1999||11:42 PM||||theogre might remember my smog test problems a few months back...<P>I had to repair a cracked egr-intake manifold tube, and I founf a vacumn fitting with a split in it.<P>My symptoms were the same as yours.... so I'd look at the tube and all of the vacumn fittings.<P>Kage||||reg||1
Z||000005||ayamnik||09-24-1999||10:08 AM||||I took my egr off to see if it was good it wasn’t it was not moving so I pushed it open with my finger and it was hard to move. After I pushed it open it didn’t close. So could this be my problem?||||reg||10
Z||000006||Lynx||09-27-1999||04:36 AM||||Could be a vaccum leak in the brake booster vaccum if the engine idle is bad when the brake is on. Or it could be the whole booster. My moms 3.0 grand am had that problem the idle would go down at a stop light intil it died. The booster was leaking vaccum.||||reg||12
Z||000007||Silver Bullet||09-27-1999||01:02 PM||||a friend of mine has a 4 banger fiero, and his car was doing something like that, but not quite as bad.  It also hesitated before 3,000rpm.  What it turned out to be was a bad PCV valve.  Check that just incase, it's only about a 3 dollar fix.||||reg||12
Z||000008||theogre||09-27-1999||07:21 PM||||a binding EGR could most definatly be a problem.... is it didn't spring right back replace it. It's heavily sprung so it should be hardish to push, but it should return instantly.||||reg||1
